32,2,1,talk,Midori,,"My findings are a bit discouraging. Joint clinics have struggled with budget and rota ownership, and shared nursing rounds lost a third of their visits to simple obstacles.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I found that a call-back trial actually reduced readmissions for the elderly, but the benefit vanished the moment the trial ended. Also, data agreements are incredibly slow.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We have a serious nursing shortage on the wards, but interestingly, the midwifery rota has some unusual slack due to falling birth numbers.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is tighter than we thought—down by a quarter—and we're now paying for floor space out of it. Also, off-site contacts bring in no regional funding.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Our facilities are at a breaking point. Parking fills up by eleven, and the booking system ignores any work that doesn't have a fixed appointment slot.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if off-site visits don't bring in funding, we have to be very careful about any program that relies on nurses leaving the hospital.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, that's a fair point. But @Misaki, the fact that readmissions dropped during the call-back trial suggests there is a real patient need for follow-up.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, the need is there, but we can't put more pressure on ward nurses. They are already being replaced by expensive agency staff.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,Exactly. We cannot afford a program that increases operational costs without a clear revenue stream or a way to utilize existing slack.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"And we can't ignore the physical limits. If a program requires more clinic slots or more parking, it might just seize up the whole system.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Midori,,It seems we need something that doesn't rely on fragile external agreements or overburdened ward staff.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If data agreements take fourteen months, any program requiring tight integration with outside surgeries is likely to stall.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, if the booking system is a bottleneck, perhaps a program that doesn't require traditional clinic slots would be better.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,I'm looking for a solution that fits the reduced budget and doesn't create a funding gap in twelve months.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. We need something that fits the current footprint of the hospital.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,pass,Midori,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
