57,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the candidates, the Perinatal Support Service seems promising because it uses the midwifery slack Misaki mentioned.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The Home Follow-Up Team aligns with the readmission data, but Midori's findings on visit completion and Shion's note on tariffs make it risky.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Misaki,,I agree with Midori. The Perinatal Support Service is the only one that doesn't add pressure to the already exhausted ward nursing staff.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Shion,,"The Day Rehabilitation Unit requires dedicated space, which Shizue says we don't have. Chronic Care Coordination sounds like a data agreement nightmare.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,The Perinatal Support Service is a good fit. It's a targeted service and doesn't seem to require the same volume of general parking as a rehab unit.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, the Home Follow-Up Team would likely fail for the same reasons the shared nursing round did—weather and locked gates.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"You're right, Midori. The operational friction is too high. The Perinatal service is a safer bet, provided the departments cooperate.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Since the midwifery rota has slack, they can actually carry the weight of the program without needing agency cover.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shion,,It's the most logical choice. It utilizes existing capacity and avoids the high costs of fitting out new floor space from a shrinking budget.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,It feels like the most harmonious choice. It supports new parents without breaking the rest of the hospital's flow.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Midori,,I am happy with this consensus. It's a supportive program that fits our current resources.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I concur. It's better to implement a sustainable service than another initiative that gets buried.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm glad we're considering the staffing reality. I'm fully in favor of the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shion,,The financial and operational risks are minimized here. I'm satisfied.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am as well. It's a gentle addition to our services.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Midori,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
